# DHF-REQ: keel/requirement-123
#
# raw/filesystem.cyclonedx.json is generated, not committed.
#
# syft records the absolute path of every component it catalogued, so the file
# states the directory of the checkout that produced it. Committing it makes the
# SBOM non-convergent: a refresh from a different worktree rewrites those paths
# with no inventory change, and a 545 KB artifact that always churns stops being
# read — which is how a real inventory change passes unexamined (keel/issue-149).
#
# Nothing downstream reads the committed copy. grype re-scans a freshly generated
# one, and linked-components.md / cve.md are what review consumes.
raw/filesystem.cyclonedx.json

# raw/cve-filesystem.json is generated, not committed (keel/ac-496).
#
# Same argument, second artifact. grype stamps descriptor.timestamp, so two runs
# of the same commit differ in that field with an identical vulnerability
# payload. The file also carries ~90 CVE publication dates, so a repository-side
# strip of the generation stamp would leave a file no shape-based guard can
# clear — the wall-clock instant and the payload dates are indistinguishable by
# form.
#
# Nothing reads the committed copy: cve.md and raw/cve-filesystem.txt are the
# rendered forms review consumes, and both are free of generation stamps.
raw/cve-filesystem.json
